WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.334
-They love you.
We love you.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.167
Welcome back. Thanks for
coming on the show, bud.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.000
-Thank you for having me back.
I've missed you.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.901
-Yeah, I know.
You did miss me.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.434
Hey, I want to talk to you,
because, obviously,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.133
you got the biggest show.
I want to get to all --

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.534
Everything.
All the shows, everything.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.801
"The Last of Us"
is a blockbuster. Congrats.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:19.200
But you are hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.467
-Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.968
-With Coldplay!
It's a big show.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.534
That's a big ticket right there.
That's a hot ticket.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.701
-Yeah, yeah.
-Are you excited?

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.434
Are you nervous?
What are you feeling?

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.133
Can I help in any way?
-Why do you ask?

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.267
[ Laughs ]
Are you nervous for me?

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.334
-Yeah, yeah, I am.
I'm really nervous for you.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:39.868
No way. I'm so --
I think you should've hosted --

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:41.200
-Ages ago?
-Yeah.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.400
-After my "Law &amp; Order" episode?
-Yes, that's exactly --

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.567
[ Laughter, cheers ]
That's exactly what I told --

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.901
I said, "Lorne, this guy's
got something, man."

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.901
Are you excited?
-I'm super excited.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.968
I think it's the top
of everybody's bucket list.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.467
Um, I am scared.

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.133
[ Laughter ]
-You are?

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.133
-There's, like,
a wall of sheer terror, I think,

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.767
that you start with, and then,
it's such a well-oiled machine.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.834
Everybody's so amazing
and talented.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:09.601
And they take these, you know,
blocks of, you know,

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:14.567
white-hot terror apart for you
with big cue cards.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.868
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.200
I want to say -- oh, yes.
So, have you practiced

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.267
blocking right now in sketches?
-Yeah, we just started some --

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.234
some blocking --
-Isn't it the most fun?

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.968
-It's a blast.
-I mean, it is a great crew.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.267
We have the best crew here, too.
-Yes, yes.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.334
-But after us,
"Saturday Night Live."

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.033
-Second to this show.
-Second to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.100
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-"SNL."

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.501
-But "SNL," it's just amazing.

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.434
And it's the last live show
on TV.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.501
Wait, "The Last of Us."

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.167
I see a connection already.
-Ah!

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.334
-Is it too late
to write that in?

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.434
-I hear clicking.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.734
If things weren't big enough
for you and your life

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:49.434
and your career,
"The Last of Us,"

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.734
it is the biggest thing
in the world.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.501
But you also have
"The Mandalorian"

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:54.868
that premieres...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:59.200
...season three, next month!

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.934
You are --
You are the Mandalorian.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.601
I know there's also
so many secrets,

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:05.767
and I don't want
to spoil anything --

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.434
-I'll tell you everything.
-No, I -- no.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:10.000
I don't want that.
But can you tell fans

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.801
anything about season three?

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.267
-I will say,
there will be more Mandalorians.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.033
[ Cheers ]
-All right, that's good.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.467
I'll take that.
-A lot of them.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:21.067
Big, epic battle.
Plural.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.968
Maybe.
-Ooh!

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:26.267
I love that.
Baby Yoda is not in this season.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.767
[ Both laugh ]
No, I'm just kidding.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.801
-They couldn't figure his
contract out for season three.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:32.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.834
They're still --
They're still in negotiations.

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.868
-Yeah, he's just
got a good agent. How is --

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.400
-His head got bigger
than his ears.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.868
-Ah, nice!
-Ah!

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.601
-How is Grogu?

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.100
What's he gonna be doing
this season?

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.334
-He's been very good.
He's still learning.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.400
-Aww.
-Teaching.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.400
-Yeah.
He is.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.234
-Protected.
Protecting.

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.334
-Yeah.
-I think if I say any more...

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.667
-Yep, don't say it.
-...I'll be replaced.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.868
Like, not just as
the Mandalorian,

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.100
but as a human being in life.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.100
-That's how powerful Disney is.
-Exactly.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.167
And their technology
is so sophisticated,

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:05.734
they'll just replace --
-A.I.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.934
-...a different Pedro Pascal,
exactly.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.734
-March 1st on Disney+,
by the way.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.167
That's when it premieres.
Congrats on that.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.567
-Thank you.
-But let's talk about this.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.767
But now, you've done that,
and it was the biggest thing,

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:18.367
and you go, "Oh, my gosh."
And then there's --

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.167
Well, let's just go back.
"Game of Thrones."

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:25.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.634
Home run.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.968
"Narcos."
"Narcos."

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.868
Home run.
Home run.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.968
"Mandalorian."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:36.667
Home run.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.400
And then "The Last of Us."
What are you ta--

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.534
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:45.000
Who -- I'm mad!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.267
-And that's the end.
-No!

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.534
It's just the beginning.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:51.601
-I'll do "SNL" and then --
you're retired, buddy.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.067
-It's just the beginning.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.634
-You forgot "Law &amp; Order: SVU."
-Yeah, I did forget that.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.400
I left that out.
But you're so talented.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.968
But this is --
This is some kind of genius move

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.033
that you've been doing.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.734
I've never seen
a career like this.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.501
-I have nothing to do it.
-Yes, you do!

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.467
How do you pick shows that are
gonna be giant hits?

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:11.100
-The door opens,
and you're like --

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.133
-No way.
-Let me in.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.167
-You're jumping in.
-I beg.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.200
-No, you don't.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.100
Like, how does
"Last of Us" come about?

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.501
Do the creators --

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.801
-That was
a really strange circumstance.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.601
I was actually in London,

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.300
and everyone else
was in Los Angeles.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.901
And I got sent these scripts
and said --

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.567
I was told that "Craig Mazin
wants you to read these scripts,

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:34.400
and if you like them,
he'd like to talk to you."

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.434
I loved "Chernobyl,"
the miniseries

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.634
that he showran for HBO.
-It was fantastic.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:42.067
-It was unbelievable.
Anyway, I read the first script,

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.267
and I was like,
"Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.501
I want to meet him,
I want to meet him."

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:47.467
-Yeah.
-And we talked, we fell in love.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:51.534
[ Laughter ]
And he --

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.868
And they were like, "Will you
stay up a little bit later?"

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:56.634
At this point, it was getting
kind of late in London --

00:04:56.634 --> 00:05:00.100
"to talk to Neil Druckmann,
the creator of the video game."

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.501
Genius.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.267
-Brilliant guy.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:06.100
"And he'd like to talk to you,
as well."

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.267
Stay up for that Zoom.
We all fall in love again.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:13.334
And then I -- and then,
at that point, it's really late.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:16.167
I've got to get up
in the morning.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:20.734
I take an Ambien to go to sleep
just in case --

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.801
they've got my adrenaline kind
of going and my -- my hopes up.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:24.968
-Yes, so you take
a sleeping pill

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:26.067
so you don't have
to think about anything.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.701
-Exactly.
So -- But I get a call,

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:32.000
and I get told that I got the
job after I took the Ambien.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.801
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.767
-And so, I was excited, I guess,
but I didn't remember.

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:37.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.501
-So, you're like,
"Was that a dream?"

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.367
-I woke up in the morning,
and the first thing

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.634
that occurred to me, was like,

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:45.634
"Oh, man.
I really want that job."

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:46.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:49.300
"And I'm in London.
They're in L.A.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.601
I'm gonna wait by the phone
all day long.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.601
This hasn't happened in a while,
you know.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.567
I'm gonna be longing,
and I'm gonna think about it

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.467
all day long."

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:59.968
-You had already got the call
that you got the job.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:02.167
-Yeah, and it's like,
"Oh, congratulations.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.167
So happy for you,"
when I looked at my phone.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.133
And I was like, "Oh, yeah!
I got the job!"

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:07.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:11.901
-"My dream is real!"

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:15.901
It is based on the awesome,
awesome, awesome video game,

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:17.400
"The Last of Us."

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.501
For those who don't know
the game or don't know the show,

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.701
how do we set it up, and how
do we set up who you play?

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.767
-I play Joel Miller.
[ Cheers ]

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.367
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:30.267
He has a bad day.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.934
Everybody -- the planet
has a really bad day.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:38.334
-Yeah.
-And a, uh...fungus, cordyceps,

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.501
finds a way to cross over
into human DNA

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:43.167
and ends the planet in 24 hours.

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:45.434
Very light, happy stuff.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:47.267
-Yeah, light.
Totally light, happy stuff.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:50.334
-A very traumatic event
shapes this man

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:53.801
into who he is 20 years later,
which is, you know,

00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:58.033
this dystopian world
with fascistic governments

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:01.000
and very contagious cordyceps

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.601
that turns you
into an infected monster.

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:06.634
It's good times.
-Yeah, it is good times.

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:09.667
Every episode, by the way,
has grown and almost like --

00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:11.534
It already was a hit,
the first episode.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:12.968
Then it's grown, second episode.

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.634
Third --
It's the biggest thing.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.567
It's getting bigger
and bigger and bigger.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:17.901
It's like --
-They know what they're doing.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.367
-Yeah, they know
what they're doing.

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:20.601
You know what you're doing,
too, bud.

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:22.133
You're fantastic.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:24.567
Here's Pedro Pascal
in this Sunday's episode

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:27.200
of "The Last of Us."
Take a look at this.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.167
-When I say go,
you crawl to that wall,

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:31.601
and you squeeze through, and you
don't come out until I say.

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.467
Okay?
[ Gunshot, glass shatters ]

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:36.934
[ Gunshots ]

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:38.267
And they're not gonna hit you.

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:39.534
Look at me!

00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:40.534
They're not gonna hit you.

00:07:40.534 --> 00:07:41.968
[ Gunshots ]

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:44.334
You stay down, you stay low,
you stay quiet.

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:46.067
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:47.100
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.067
[ Gunshots ]

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:51.234
-Go!

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:56.200
[ Gunshots ]

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.033
♪♪

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:03.501
[ Gunshots ]

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:08.133
♪♪

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:09.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:09.434 --> 00:08:11.734
-Pedro Pascal, everybody!

00:08:11.734 --> 00:08:15.000
"The Last of Us"
airs Sundays at 9:00 p.m.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.267
on HBO and HBO Max.
And this weekend, catch him

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:22.300
hosting "Saturday Night Live"
with Coldplay!

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.834
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.968
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back!

